            <ArticleTitle>Cardiovascular MRI: current role in patient management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>589-606</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The role of cardiovascular MRI in patient management is still evolving. Its capability to demonstrate anatomy without risk has made it an important supplement to ultrasound and a replacement for CT and angiography in many settings. In vivo metabolic studies of congenital and acquired diseases may be the most important future developments.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
